# Docker reads no global excludes, so every dot path at any depth is kept out,
# a nested repository's .git with it, and the project's own are let back in by
# name. Letting .github in lets in all it holds, so a dot path below it is kept
# out again last. A Compose override holds a checkout's settings, not the tree's.
**/.*
/docker-compose.*.yml
/tmp/

!/.env.example
!/.github
!/.hadolint.yaml
!/.mdformat.toml
!/.shellcheckrc
!/.yamllint.yaml
/.github/**/.*
